# Munshot — local environment. Copy to `.env` (gitignored) and fill in.
#
# SUMMARIES — /api/summary needs EITHER an OpenAI key OR an Anthropic key
# (whichever is set is auto-detected and used).

# OpenAI — https://platform.openai.com/api-keys (starts with "sk-")
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Anthropic — https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys (starts with "sk-ant-")
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Optional model override. Defaults: OpenAI → gpt-4o-mini, Anthropic → claude-opus-4-8
# SUMMARY_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini

# TRANSCRIPTION (optional) — used only for shows WITHOUT a transcript in their feed.
# Provider chain: feed transcript (free) → Groq (free, short episodes) → Deepgram (any length)

# Deepgram — transcribes long episodes (URL-based, any length). https://console.deepgram.com
DEEPGRAM_API_KEY=
# DEEPGRAM_MODEL=nova-3

# Groq free-tier Whisper (short episodes) — https://console.groq.com/keys (starts with "gsk_")
GROQ_API_KEY=

# MEMBER FEEDS (optional) — paid episodes in the AUTOMATED Monday digest.
#
# You do NOT need this for normal use: paste your member feed URL in Discover and
# it's stored with your tracked shows, so the app fetches your paid episodes for
# you. The one thing that can't see it is the digest cron — it has no user session
# and builds ONE shared edition from the seed shows. This is how a member feed
# reaches that.
#
# Format: <seedShowId>=<feedUrl>, comma- or newline-separated. Several feeds for
# one show are pooled (Stratechery's Passport podcast feed carries the audio, its
# rss feed the full article text — both is better than either).
#
# ⚠ Single-tenant deployments only. The seed episode list is shared by everyone
#   using the space, so a member feed here shows one subscriber's paid content to
#   every visitor — and redistributes what the publisher sold to one person.
#   Leave unset on anything multi-customer. Rotate the token if it ever leaks.
# MEMBER_FEEDS=stratechery=https://<publisher>.passport.online/feed/podcast/<token>
